HST Office on Windows: own AppUserModelIDs, so taskbar groups, pinned items and jump lists are not shared with LibreOffice.

Both suites used TheDocumentFoundation.LibreOffice.<Module> as the Windows AppUserModelID. With both
installed, the taskbar grouped their windows together, a pinned item could start the other suite,
and the jump lists (recent documents) mixed both suites' files.

Every place that sets or consumes the id now uses HASONTECH.HSTOffice.<Module> (Writer, Calc,
Impress, Draw, Math, Base, Startcenter, SafeMode):
- framework titlebarupdate: the per-module id set on each window (vcl/win salframe property store);
- vcl/win salinst: SHAddToRecentDocs (SHARD_APPIDINFO), so recent documents go to the HST jump list;
- shell/source/win32 jumplist: the jump-list API;
- scp2: the Start menu shortcuts' System.AppUserModel.ID and the ProgIDs' AppUserModelID values, so
  pinned shortcuts and file-type activations match the running windows.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0).

--- a/framework/source/helper/titlebarupdate.cxx
+++ b/framework/source/helper/titlebarupdate.cxx
@@ -146,7 +146,7 @@
             sDesktopName = "Startcenter";
 #if defined(_WIN32)
         // We use a hardcoded product name matching the registry keys so applications can be associated with file types
-        sApplicationID = "TheDocumentFoundation.LibreOffice." + sDesktopName;
+        sApplicationID = "HASONTECH.HSTOffice." + sDesktopName;
 #else
         // HST Office: the launcher id (vn.hasontech.hstoffice-<module>, the launchers' StartupWMClass),
         // not "<product>-<module>", so HST windows never take LibreOffice's launcher.
--- a/scp2/inc/macros.inc
